# AGENTS.md

This file is generated by `nise agents`. It is Nise-owned: regenerating it
overwrites this file, and hand edits are lost. Edit `nise.json` and re-run
`nise agents` instead of changing this document directly; see
[Files you must not hand-edit](#files-you-must-not-hand-edit) below.

## Stack

- Profile: `go-chi-postgres-svelte` — Go, chi, PostgreSQL (pgx, sqlc, Goose), and a
  statically built SvelteKit frontend embedded in the compiled binary.
- Generated or last upgraded by nise CLI version `v0.0.0-golden`.
- Targets Nise runtime package version `v0.1.0`.
- Selected modules: notifications, organizations, totp, uploads.

## Directory layout and ownership

`app` means the application owns the directory: nise writes it once (or
not at all) and never overwrites your edits there. `nise` means nise owns
it: it is regenerated, and hand edits are lost.

| Path | Owner | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `api/` | app | The authoritative OpenAPI document (api/openapi.yaml); hand-edited from generation onward. |
| `cmd/<app>/` | app | Application entry point: flag parsing and process-mode selection, calling internal/app. |
| `db/` | nise | db/embed.go embeds db/migrations/*.sql into the binary. |
| `db/migrations/` | app | Sequential, hand-written SQL migrations, NNNNN_snake_case.sql. |
| `deploy/` | app | Dockerfile, local compose file, and deployment notes. |
| `frontend/` | app | SvelteKit project; contains no Go files. frontend/src/lib/api/schema.d.ts is the one Nise-owned file in this tree, regenerated from api/openapi.yaml. |
| `internal/app/` | app | Explicit constructor wiring and process-mode selection; internal/app/modules.gen.go is Nise-owned and regenerated as the module selection changes. |
| `internal/features/` | app | One vertical slice per feature: domain rules, use cases, handlers, SQL, and tests. Each feature's store/ subdirectory is Nise-owned sqlc output. |
| `internal/platform/config/` | app | Typed configuration built over runtime/config. |
| `internal/platform/database/` | app | pgxpool setup and the Goose migration runner. |
| `internal/platform/httpapi/` | app | Router and middleware order; internal/platform/httpapi/openapigen/ is Nise-owned oapi-codegen output. |
| `internal/platform/jobs/` | app | The River job runner, its queues, and their registration. A job's payload and business rules belong to the feature that enqueues it. |
| `internal/platform/mail/` | app | The mail interface, SMTP transport, and templates. A message's content belongs to the feature that sends it. |
| `internal/platform/webui/` | nise | Embeds the built frontend and serves the SPA; internal/platform/webui/embedded/client/ is pnpm build output and is not committed. |

Ownership is also readable from the path, wherever it appears: the
directory names `store/`, `openapigen/`, and `embedded/`, and any file
ending `.gen.go`, are always regenerated Nise output. The same layout,
with the full rationale, is documented at [Generated application
layout](https://github.com/drilonrecica/nise-and-go/blob/main/docs/generated-application-layout.md).

The machine-readable form of this same table, plus this project's module
selection, is `.nise/architecture.json` (schema version 1), alongside this file.

## Files you must not hand-edit

These carry the `Code generated by nise; DO NOT EDIT.` header (or, for a
JSON file, a `generated` field saying the same thing) and are overwritten
on every regeneration:

- `AGENTS.md` and `.nise/architecture.json` — this file and its machine-readable sibling
- `nise.json` — the project recipe
- `internal/app/modules.gen.go`
- `internal/platform/httpapi/openapigen/**`
- `internal/features/<feature>/store/**`
- `internal/platform/webui/embedded/client/**` — build output; not committed
- `frontend/src/lib/api/schema.d.ts`

## Build, test, and lint

`frontend/` sits inside this Go module, so a bare `./...` also walks
`frontend/node_modules/`. Name the Go targets explicitly instead:

```sh
go build ./cmd/... ./internal/... ./db/...
go test ./cmd/... ./internal/... ./db/...
go vet ./cmd/... ./internal/... ./db/...
gofmt -l cmd internal db
```

Frontend:

```sh
pnpm --dir frontend install
pnpm --dir frontend check
pnpm --dir frontend build
```

## Non-negotiable conventions

- Svelte components use Svelte 5 runes (`$state`, `$derived`, `$effect`) only — no Svelte 4 reactive statements (`$:`) and no store-as-primary-state.
- A use case owns its transaction boundary. Handlers do transport work only; the `store` package runs queries and never begins a business transaction on its own.
- Authorization defaults to deny. A missing or unevaluated permission check is a bug, not an implicit allow.
- Input decoding is strict: an unknown field or a type mismatch is rejected, not ignored.
- No new dependency is added to `go.mod` or `frontend/package.json` without a documented, concrete reason.

